    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-048: Flex Wrap (Multi-line Flex)**. **Documentation only.** Implementation (3 commits, ~300 lines) lands in a follow-up PR.\n\n**Closes ADR-029's biggest deferral.** `flex-wrap: wrap` has been parsed since ADR-029 (into `ComputedStyle` via shorthand expansion) but treated as `nowrap` by the layout engine. This ADR implements the multi-line algorithm.\n\n## Measurement (2026-10-29)\n\n| Value | Uses |\n|---|---|\n| `flex-wrap: wrap` | 3 |\n| `flex-wrap: nowrap` | 3 |\n\nAll 3 wrap rules are `.mw-header { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 16px }` variants.\n\n## Honest scoping: zero first-viewport delta\n\nTwo independent conditions unmet today:\n\n1. **`.mw-header` not in current fetched HTML** — exact-class DOM walk: `mw-header NOT FOUND`. The rule exists in CSS but has no element to match.\n2. **At viewport ≥ 1680px, `.mw-header` uses `display: grid`** — the `@media (min-width: 1680px)` override wins. Flex only applies below 1680px.\n\nThe header will reappear in a future snapshot (Wikipedia hasn't removed it — likely a mobile-layout snapshot), and any viewport < 1680px hits the flex rule immediately.\n\n**Verification is synthetic-DOM only.** Same category as ADR-041 Commit 1 (pseudo parse shipped before synthesis could render) and ADR-047 (mask paint shipped before any visible consumer).\n\n## Scope\n\n### Commit 1 — Refactor (behavior-neutral)\n- Extract Phases B–E of `layout_flex_children` into `resolve_flex_line()` helper\n- Call helper once for `flex-wrap: nowrap`\n- **Byte-identical single-line output** — all 20 ADR-029 flex tests pass unchanged\n- Zero new tests; zero visible delta\n\n### Commit 2 — Multi-line wrap\n- Break `fcs` into lines by accumulated `basis + gap` vs `content_w`\n- Per-line `resolve_flex_line` calls\n- Line stacking with `row_gap` (gap fallback)\n- Container main = max(line widths), cross = sum(line heights) + (N-1) * row_gap\n- 15+ synthetic-DOM tests\n- No PNG gate possible (no consumer)\n\n### Commit 3 — Docs\n- ADR-048 → Implemented with zero-delta caveat\n- Post-ADR-048 note in ADR-029 (deferral closed)\n- README + CHANGELOG\n\n## Deferred (per ADR)\n\n- **`align-content`** (parsing + cross-axis distribution) — lines pack tight, no stretch. Zero consumers today.\n- `flex-wrap: wrap-reverse` (0 uses)\n- `flex-direction: column` + wrap (0 uses)\n- Cross-axis shrink of items that can't fit alone (CSS §9.3)\n- `gap: <a> <b>` two-value cross-axis interpretation (v1 uses first token for both axes)\n\n## Reviewer checklist\n\n- [ ] **Extract helper in Commit 1** — Phases B–E into `resolve_flex_line()`. Byte-identical output proven by 20 existing flex tests. Alternative (duplicate algorithm inline for wrap) rejected — 200 lines of near-duplicate code that would drift.\n- [ ] **`align-content` deferred** — parsing + distribution with zero consumers is speculative work. Same trap ADR-043 avoided.\n- [ ] **Row-only wrap** — `.mw-header` is row-direction; column-wrap deferred. Keeps line-breaking logic to one axis.\n- [ ] **`gap` first-token-only for cross axis** — `.mw-header { gap: 16px }` is single-value, so this is fine. Two-value `gap` deferred (0 uses).\n- [ ] **Zero first-viewport delta is honestly framed** — no PNG gate possible. Synthetic-DOM tests are the verification category. Same as ADR-041 Commit 1 and ADR-047.\n\n## Test plan\n\nNo code touched. Post-merge: `cmake --build build && ./build/tests/honeybee_tests` — 598 / 2307 unchanged.\n\n## ADR\n\n`docs/decisions/048-flex-wrap.md` — status Accepted; implementation in follow-up PR.\n\nRefs #226\n",
